# retry_bounded — bounded retry of a fallible call (R-041). `useRetry 3` on a
# call wraps it in a retry loop: the fallible out-param call is re-invoked until
# it returns ok (status 0) or the attempt budget is spent. The demo symbol
# `ss_ffi_count` increments a counter, writes it through the out-pointer, and
# ALWAYS returns an error status — so with `useRetry 3` it is invoked exactly 3
# times and the written value is 3, proving the retry re-invoked the call. When
# the budget is exhausted the last error surfaces normally (catch / branch
# ifError). This exercises:
#   * retry count: the call runs 3 times (out == 3), not once;
#   * exhaustion: after 3 failed attempts the error is delivered, not swallowed.
# Expected output: 3 PASS lines then  ---- 3 passed, 0 failed ----

RetryBounded is project
RetryBounded module examplesRetryBounded
RetryBounded target console
RetryBounded entry main

examplesRetryBounded is module
examplesRetryBounded path examples.retryBounded
examplesRetryBounded exports main
examplesRetryBounded purpose "Retry a flaky call a bounded number of times and assert the count"
examplesRetryBounded invariant "The call runs exactly the retry budget; the final error surfaces"

ExitCode is alias
ExitCode for Int32
ExitCode purpose "Process exit status"

RetryError is error
RetryError purpose "The flaky call's error status after the retry budget is spent"

stdoutWriter is capability
stdoutWriter grants write console.stdout
stdoutWriter purpose "Allow controlled writes to standard output"

ffiCount is operation
ffiCount out Int64
ffiCount body runtimeBinding ss_ffi_count
ffiCount outParam
ffiCount purpose "Increment and return a per-process call counter; always fails"
ffiCount invariant "Writes the attempt number through the out-pointer; returns non-zero"
ffiCount suppress SS5000 because "retry demo; the real home is a .semsig-backed stdlib module"

main is operation
main out ExitCode
main effect write console.stdout
main uses stdoutWriter
main async no
main purpose "Retry a flaky call three times and assert it ran three times"
main invariant "All three assertions hold"
main let three immutable Int64 3
main let oneGuard immutable Int64 1
main let oneMark immutable Int64 1
main let errFlag mutable Int64 0
main let tnCount immutable String "useRetry 3 invokes the flaky call exactly 3 times"
main let tnRetried immutable String "the call retried beyond the first attempt (not 1)"
main let tnExhausted immutable String "after the budget is spent the error surfaces (caught)"
main do retryCall
main branch ifError retryCall goto errCaught
main goto afterErr
main at errCaught set errFlag oneMark
main at afterErr do checkCount
main do checkRetried
main do checkExhausted
main do harnessReport
main return harnessSummaryCode

retryCall is call
retryCall in main
retryCall invokes ffiCount
retryCall out attempts Int64
retryCall catch retryErr RetryError
retryCall useRetry 3

checkCount is call
checkCount in main
checkCount invokes test.assertEqualInt64
checkCount arg name String tnCount
checkCount arg expected Int64 three
checkCount arg actual Int64 attempts

checkRetried is call
checkRetried in main
checkRetried invokes test.assertNotEqualInt64
checkRetried arg name String tnRetried
checkRetried arg expected Int64 oneGuard
checkRetried arg actual Int64 attempts

checkExhausted is call
checkExhausted in main
checkExhausted invokes test.assertEqualInt64
checkExhausted arg name String tnExhausted
checkExhausted arg expected Int64 oneMark
checkExhausted arg actual Int64 errFlag

harnessReport is call
harnessReport in main
harnessReport invokes test.summary
harnessReport out harnessSummaryCode ExitCode
